John Gibson wrote:
>
> A group of Stone giants appeared while I was clearing out Sokoban. 
> Although they did not disturb any of the existing boulders, a few of 
> them were generated with boulders of their own.  Naturally when I killed 
> them I was left with an unsolvable puzzle (until I smashed a boulder or 
> two).  Is this the intended behavior (forcing the player to take a luck 
> penalty)?

This is a good reason to finish Sokoban early in the game.  The level
of monsters generated on a level is based on the average of your current
level and the depth.  Do Sokoban while inexperienced and the chances of
getting giants is very low.  Put off doing Sokoban until you are Quest
qualified and you run that risk.  To me, this is an intended feature.
It is part of why I prefer to do Sokoban about the same time as mine
town or mines end.

If you're not playing atheist, any amount of luck penalty is temporary
and it can be repaired.

